\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Lemma}
\title{Ordered products of negative Clifford generators}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{Let #{n\ge1}. In the real unital associative algebra presented by
#{d_1,\ldots,d_n} with #{d_j^2=-1} and
#{d_i d_j=-d_j d_i} for #{i\ne j}, the ordered products on
subsets of the axes, including #{1}, form a basis. The even and odd lengths give a grading by parity.
A nonzero product of vectors has the parity of its number of
factors.
On the real span of the generators use the inner product for
which they are orthonormal. For a product #{a} of #{p} unit
vectors the action
##{v\longmapsto(-1)^p a v a^{-1}}
is a composition of #{p} orthogonal reflections.}

\proof{
\p{Interchange unequal neighboring indices and remove repeated
pairs using the relations. This gives spanning. For independence,
let #{d_j} act on the real exterior algebra of #{\mathbb R^n} by
wedging on the left with the #{j}th unit vector minus contracting
with that vector. On an ordered exterior basis element with
index set #{I} this toggles #{j} with sign
#{(-1)^{|\{i\in I:i<j\}|}} when inserting and the opposite sign
when deleting. Toggling twice gives minus the identity. For two
distinct indices, toggling the smaller changes the insertion or
deletion sign at the larger while the reverse change leaves the
smaller sign alone. Thus these operators satisfy the defining
relations. The ordered products on distinct subsets take the
exterior unit to distinct exterior basis vectors. This proves
independence. Multiplication preserves the sum of lengths modulo
two. The even and odd spans have zero intersection, so a nonzero
homogeneous product has a unique parity.}

\p{For unit #{w} in the real vector span the relations give
#{w^2=-1} and #{wv+vw=-2\langle w,v\rangle}.
Thus #{-w v w^{-1}=v-2\langle w,v\rangle w}, reflection across
the hyperplane perpendicular to #{w}. Conjugations compose and
their scalar signs multiply, giving the stated action.}
}

\p{The exterior-unit calculation also appears for general
bilinear forms in \ref{fdip-00QB}. For an orthogonal basis, TauCeti's
\leanref/tauceti{CliffordAlgebra.basis_eq_prod_map_sort}
identifies the element indexed by a finite subset with its
increasing product. With quadratic form #{v\mapsto-\langle v,v\rangle},
\<html:span>[class]{lean-ref}{[\code{CliffordAlgebra.pinToOrthogonal_ι_apply}](https://taucetiproject.github.io/TauCeti/docs/find/#doc/CliffordAlgebra.pinToOrthogonal_\%25CE\%25B9_apply)}
gives the reflection from a vector of quadratic value #{-1}.
It acts on vectors by signed conjugation.}
